## Context
Code review issue #8 from stage6-style-fix-review.md

## Problem
No try-catch around `getStylePrompt()` call in generator-section.ts. If the function throws unexpectedly, the entire section generation fails without graceful fallback.

```typescript
// packages/course-gen-platform/src/stages/stage6-lesson-content/nodes/generator/generator-section.ts:92
const stylePrompt = getStylePrompt(style);
```

## Solution
Wrap in try-catch with fallback to default style:

```typescript
import { DEFAULT_COURSE_STYLE } from '@megacampus/shared-types';

let stylePrompt: string;
try {
  stylePrompt = getStylePrompt(style);
} catch (error) {
  logger.warn(
    { style, error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error) },
    'Failed to get style prompt, using default'
  );
  stylePrompt = getStylePrompt(DEFAULT_COURSE_STYLE);
}
```

## Files to modify
- `packages/course-gen-platform/src/stages/stage6-lesson-content/nodes/generator/generator-section.ts`

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] getStylePrompt wrapped in try-catch
- [ ] Warning logged on failure with style value
- [ ] Falls back to DEFAULT_COURSE_STYLE
- [ ] Type-check passes

