## Root Cause
Jina API has a limit of 2 concurrent requests. In quality-validator.ts:322-325, Promise.all makes 2 parallel generateEmbedding calls INSIDE a for loop, which can exceed the limit if the loop iterates before previous calls complete.

## Files to modify
1. packages/course-gen-platform/src/shared/embeddings/jina-client.ts
   - Add ConcurrencyLimiter class with semaphore pattern (max 2 concurrent)
   - Wrap makeJinaRequest with concurrency control

## Implementation
Add semaphore-based concurrency limiter:
```typescript
class ConcurrencyLimiter {
  private running = 0;
  private queue: (() => void)[] = [];
  constructor(private maxConcurrent: number = 2) {}

  async acquire(): Promise<void> {
    if (this.running < this.maxConcurrent) {
      this.running++;
      return;
    }
    return new Promise(resolve => this.queue.push(resolve));
  }

  release(): void {
    this.running--;
    if (this.queue.length > 0) {
      this.running++;
      this.queue.shift()!();
    }
  }
}
```

Apply in makeJinaRequest:
```typescript
const concurrencyLimiter = new ConcurrencyLimiter(2);

async function makeJinaRequest(payload: JinaEmbeddingRequest): Promise<JinaEmbeddingResponse> {
  validateJinaConfig();
  await concurrencyLimiter.acquire();
  try {
    await rateLimiter.waitForSlot();
    // ... existing fetch logic
  } finally {
    concurrencyLimiter.release();
  }
}
```

## From Code Review ISSUE-1

Remove `as unknown as JobHandler` casts in processor.ts by creating proper adapter types.

## Current Problem
All handlers use `as unknown as` casts, bypassing TypeScript safety:
```typescript
const jobHandlers: Record<string, JobHandler> = {
  [JobType.TEST_JOB]: testJobHandler as unknown as JobHandler,
  // ... etc
};
```

## Solution Options

### Option 1: Adapter wrapper
```typescript
function adaptHandler<T extends JobData>(handler: BaseJobHandler<T>): SandboxedJobHandler<T> {
  return {
    process: async (job: SandboxedJob<T>) => {
      return handler.process(job as unknown as Job<T>);
    },
  };
}
```

### Option 2: Shared MinimalJob interface
Create interface that both Job and SandboxedJob satisfy.

